# SHIFTAVG:  Average of X_ram shifted files (fnnthin 2:5 - fnrefin 2:5) to stdout for gnuplot.
# Scott.D.Thomas@nasa.gov, Dell Services Federal Government, Oct 2011 - Jan 2013
# ACITS2 Contract NNA08AF13C, Task 335/385/924, NASA Ames Research Center
# 
# Usage:  shiftavg [-debug] [-debug=n] [-h|-H] [-pct] [beg end ref]
# 
# The -debug option causes all the corrected and shifted (xshif,dPPrc) to be written.
#  If -debug=n appears, where n is a positive integer, then -debug and only draw the nth and quit after the nth debug output.
# 
# The -h option makes the waterfall plots subtract a correction based on h_nose and h_nose at X_ramMin
# The -H option uses h_nose at X_ramMax.
# 
# The -pct option computes the average and sigma at points n * 0.01
# that cover the x range of values, e.g. -110.00, -109.99, -109.98, ....
# 
# If the three integers beg end ref do not appear on the command line, then the
# program will prompt for the reference .txt file and then the data .txt file names.
# 
# If a .txt file is not found, skip it.
# 
# The program expects all .txt files to have same number of data values, else fatal error.
# 
# Command line:  shiftavg -pct
# Enter name of csv2gnu .txt file to use as reference.
# LM3r0221.txt
# Enter names of csv2gnu .txt file to correct and shift for the average.
